cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "Verification scripts for: Two-basepoint Terwilliger algebras and the quantum rigidity of circulant graphs of prime order"
abstract: >-
  Exact-arithmetic verification of the computational claims of the paper
  "Two-basepoint Terwilliger algebras and the quantum rigidity of circulant
  graphs of prime order": the four capture certificates, the confinement lemma
  and quadratic threshold, the saturation of the two-basepoint module for all
  214 pairs (p,E) with p <= 250, and the capture-depth table of Appendix A.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Marashdeh
    given-names: Mohammad F.
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics, Mutah University, Karak, Jordan"
    email: marashdeh@mutah.edu.jo
license: MIT
keywords:
  - quantum automorphism group
  - quantum permutation group
  - circulant graph
  - Paley graph
  - Terwilliger algebra
  - cyclotomic association scheme
